## Scenario

Management suspects that an employee is using Tor Browser to bypass organizational network restrictions. The investigation examines installer activity, browser execution, network connections, and related file artifacts to reconstruct the sequence of events.

The scenario represents a simulated acceptable-use policy violation. Activity was performed on a controlled lab endpoint.

## Investigation Objectives

- Identify Tor Browser installer acquisition and execution.
- Identify Tor Browser components and associated processes.
- Investigate network connections attributed to those processes.
- Examine the lifecycle of a scenario-specific text file.
- Correlate events into a chronological investigation timeline.
- Document findings and appropriate response recommendations.

## Activity Performed

1. Downloaded Tor Browser from the [official Tor Project website](https://www.torproject.org/download/).
2. Executed the installer on `jh-tor-hunt-01`.
3. Launched Tor Browser from its installation directory.
4. Connected to Tor and browsed websites to generate network telemetry.
5. Created the desktop text file `tor-shopping-list.txt` with fictional test entries.
6. Deleted the text file to generate additional file activity.

### Silent Installation Test Command

```powershell
.\tor-browser-windows-x86_64-portable-15.0.20.exe /S
```

The process command line provides the evidence needed to determine whether the silent-installation switch was used during a particular execution.

